  "abstract": {
    "value": "The prevalence of 1,3-dienes as substrates in some of the most important transformations in organic synthesis (e.g. Diels– Alder reactions) engenders this class of compounds as highly sought after raw materials for carbon–carbon bond construction. In addition, nature has incorporated 1,3-dienes into a multitude of biologically active natural products, thus further solidifying the broad interest of this functional group beyond simple methodology development. Nonetheless, despite their pervasiveness and significant efforts from the synthetic community, the stereoselective synthesis of functionalized, highly substituted 1,3-dienes remains a formidable challenge.<sup>[1–4]</sup>",
